          %h2#the_knot_group_of_a_knot The Knot Group of a Knot
          %p
            The
            = succeed "," do
              %strong knot group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(K)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knot"} knot
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knot+complement"} complement of the knot
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            as the image of the embedding rather than the embedding itself. We can therefore write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ∖
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3 \setminus K
            for the space outside the knot, i.e. its complement. This is clearly arcwise connected so we do not need to worry about a choice of base point any point will do. We make the
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(K) \coloneqq \pi_1(\mathbb{R}^3 \setminus K)
              \.
          %p
            To see that this is an invariant of the knot type, note that if you perform an ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotopy"} isotopy
            on the knot then it deforms this complement into the complement of the isotopic knot.
          %p
            This is an unambiguous definition, but does not tell us how to calculate anything about this group for a given knot. Luckily there are two neat algorithms for giving
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+presentation"} presentations
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(K)
            for arbitrary knots working from a diagram of that knot, one due to Wirtinger, the other to Dehn.
          %h2#the_dehn_presentation The Dehn Presentation
          %p
            Start by orienting the knot diagram. The diagram divides the plane into various faces. Label these faces with distinct letters. For example,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1,\ldots, x_n
          %p A typical crossing will have a configuration something like this:
          %div{:style => "text-align:center"}
            %svg{:height => "214", "se:nonce" => "75641", :width => "214", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:se" => "http://svg-edit.googlecode.com"}
              %g
                %title Layer 1
                %line#svg_75641_1{:fill => "none", "marker-end" => "url(#se_marker_end_svg_75641_1)", :stroke => "#7f0000", "stroke-width" => "4", :x1 => "102", :x2 => "102", :y1 => "214", :y2 => "14"}
                %rect#svg_75641_3{:fill => "#ffffff", :height => "17", :stroke => "#7f0000", "stroke-width" => "0", :width => "43", :x => "81", :y => "106"}
                %line#svg_75641_2{:fill => "none", "marker-end" => "url(#se_marker_end_svg_75641_2)", :stroke => "#7f0000", "stroke-width" => "4", :x1 => "2", :x2 => "202", :y1 => "114", :y2 => "114"}
                %foreignobject#svg_75641_4{"font-size" => "20", :height => "50", :width => "50", :x => "27", :y => "39"}
                  %math{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i
                %foreignobject#svg_75641_5{"font-size" => "20", :height => "50", :width => "50", :x => "27", :y => "164"}
                  %math{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_j
                %foreignobject#svg_75641_13{"font-size" => "20", :height => "50", :width => "50", :x => "127", :y => "39"}
                  %math{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi l
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_l
                %foreignobject#svg_75641_21{"font-size" => "20", :height => "50", :width => "50", :x => "127", :y => "164"}
                  %math{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_k
              %defs
                %marker#se_marker_end_svg_75641_1{:markerheight => "5", :markerunits => "strokeWidth", :markerwidth => "5", :orient => "auto", :refx => "50", :refy => "50", :viewbox => "0 0 100 100"}
                  %path#svg_75641_6{:d => "m100,50l-100,40l30,-40l-30,-40l100,40z", :fill => "#7f0000", :stroke => "#7f0000", "stroke-width" => "10"}
                %marker#se_marker_end_svg_75641_2{:markerheight => "5", :markerunits => "strokeWidth", :markerwidth => "5", :orient => "auto", :refx => "50", :refy => "50", :viewbox => "0 0 100 100"}
                  %path#svg_75641_7{:d => "m100,50l-100,40l30,-40l-30,-40l100,40z", :fill => "#7f0000", :stroke => "#7f0000", "stroke-width" => "10"}
          %p
            Look at the underpass arc that leaves the crossing, and write down the face labels going anticlockwise around the crossing, and alternating in exponent between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +1
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %msubsup
                      %mi x
                      %mi j
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi k
                    %msubsup
                      %mi x
                      %mi l
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i x_j^{-1}x_k x_l^{-1}
            %em one
            face label to be
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %p
            That method gives the following presentation, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_m
            is the choice of generator to be set to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mtext relations from crossings
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi m
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle x_1, \ldots, x_n\mid \text{relations from crossings}, x_m=1\rangle.
          %p
            This is a presentation of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(K)
          %p
            The element in the fundamental group corresponding to a particular face is given as follows. We set the basepoint to a point above the plane and draw a path which goes from the basepoint and through the face. It then goes under the plane (thus, under the knot) to the face whose label was set to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %h2#example_of_a_dehn_presentation Example of a Dehn presentation
          %p
            We will calculate the Dehn presentation for the cinquefoil knot. This is the next knot in the family of
            = succeed "-torus" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,k)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trefoil+knot"} trefoil knot
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            up to
